\uline{$4$ types of elementary paths}$^{*}$

a) ``quarter twist'' $(2\times3\times4)$ (contour of a hole)

b) ``sixth of a turn'' $(2\times2\times3)$ (on equator)

c) pole to hole $(2\times2\times3)$ and conversely

d) pole to equator and conversely $(2\times2\times3)$

$2$ additional composite types

e) hole to hole $(2\times3)$ or ``third of a turn''

f) half twist $(2\times2\times3)$

[and of course, g) full twist $2\times2\times3)$]

